codemap 8
path gui-widgets
kind layer
author ai
group gui
note The handful of widgets the GUI is written in. There is no widget library under this: each one is a function on App that opens an element or two with the right colours and returns what the element tree says the mouse did to it. They exist because the same three lines were being written everywhere, not because anything needed abstracting - which is why there are seven of them and why a panel that wants something else just opens elements directly. The theme is a dozen constants in one place, and the only piece with state is the text field, since a caret and a history cannot be derived from anything.

